  "result": "Excellent! All 334 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Summary\n\nCreated a new `src/export.js` module with the `exportCsv()` function that exports invoices as CSV with the following features:\n\n### CSV Format:\n- **Header**: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n- **Data**: One line per invoice in the order given\n- **Amounts**: Plain euros with 2 decimals and dot separator (e.g., `1234.56`)\n  - No currency symbol (\u20ac)\n  - No thousands separator\n- **CSV Escaping**: Fields with commas, quotes, or newlines are quoted; quotes inside are doubled per RFC 4180\n- **Line endings**: LF (`\\n`)\n\n### Implementation Details:\n- `formatEurosPlain()`: Converts cents to euros string format (e.g., 123456 \u2192 \"1234.56\")\n- `escapeCsvField()`: Handles CSV escaping with proper quote doubling\n- Looks up customer names using `getCustomer()`\n- Calculates totals using `invoiceTotals()` and due amounts using `balanceDue()`\n- Rounds all amounts to integer cents before formatting\n\n### Test Coverage (34 tests):\n- Empty invoices, single and multiple invoices\n- Customer name lookup and special character handling\n- Number formatting (2 decimals, dot separator, no thousands separator)\n- CSV quoting and quote escaping\n- Field inclusion and order verification\n- Invoice status handling (draft with empty number, issued, partially paid, paid)\n- Discount and VAT handling\n- Large invoice lists\n\n**Test results:** All 334 tests pass (300 existing + 34 exportCsv tests).",
